{"type": "message", "id": "95f15f1c", "parentId": "fa901e98", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T17:59:43.541Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Given the time constraints and the difficulty of getting exact monthly data for all exchanges, let me take a pragmatic approach. I have some data points and I'll try to compile the table from the best available sources. Let me search for a few more key data points and then compile the table.\n\nLet me try to get the data from Wikipedia for each exchange and from the sources I've already found.\n\nLet me also try to get data from the HKEX Stock Connect page which has SSE and SZSE data too.\n\nActually, let me think about what data I have and what I still need. I'll compile the data from all available sources.\n\nFrom the data I've gathered:\n\n\nNow I'm reviewing the monthly S&P 500 values from multpl.com spanning January through May 2025, which gives me the closing prices for each month. I'm also pulling in additional exchange data from economyinsights.com to fill in the gaps.\n\nLooking at the NYSE metrics, I see they have around $44.7 trillion in market cap as of December 2025 with roughly 2,200 to 2,400 listed stocks and monthly trading volume around $2.7 trillion. For NASDAQ, the market cap sits at approximately $42.2 trillion with about 3,900 to 4,100 listings and similar monthly trading activity.\n\nThe Shanghai Stock Exchange has a much smaller market cap of $8.92 trillion with around 2,269 listed companies, while the Hong Kong Exchange shows $6.17 trillion in market cap across 2,600 to 2,700 listed stocks with monthly volume around $762 billion. The Shenzhen Stock Exchange is significantly smaller at roughly $3.48 trillion in market cap.\n\nNow I'm looking at the monthly trading volumes for NASDAQ's European equity operations throughout 2025, which show considerable variation from a low of about $42.6 billion in February to a peak of $59.2 billion in April.\n\nLooking at the HKEX metrics, I can see the number of listed companies has grown modestly from 2,632 in February 2025 to 2,700 by February 2026, while market capitalization has expanded significantly from HK$39.1 trillion to HK$49.9 trillion. The Hang Seng Index has also moved upward to 26,630.54 by February 2026.\n\nFor the SSE, I have December 2025 data showing a market cap of 15.15 trillion RMB, but I need to search for the January through May 2025 figures to complete the comparison. I should also check the HKEX Stock Connect page since it might contain the Shanghai and Shenzhen exchange statistics I'm looking for.\n\nLet me do a few more targeted searches to gather the remaining data points, then I'll have enough to compile a complete table with estimates where exact figures aren't available from the sources I can access.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Let me try a few more targeted searches to fill in data gaps."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_b28d7f67af2c44c382bc49f7", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"count": 5, "query": "global stock exchange monthly statistics 2025 NYSE NASDAQ market cap listed companies trading value each month"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_57a523a34a6c4eb2a0d6e6df", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"count": 5, "query": "Shanghai Stock Exchange SSE listed companies number 2025 monthly \"2,271\" OR \"2,276\" OR \"2,280\" OR \"2,285\""}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "openrouter", "model": "xiaomi/mimo-v2-pro", "usage": {"input": 1553, "output": 1423, "cacheRead": 111616, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 114592, "cost": {"input": 0.001553, "output": 0.004269, "cacheRead": 0.022323199999999998, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0281452}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775584767217, "responseId": "gen-1775584769-AtteJCn83NSASrIMmNFj"}}
